[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 17: offset QPSK.
# OQPSK delays the quadrature stream by half a symbol, so I and Q never change at the same instant and the phase moves by at most 90 degrees per step. Compare the PAPR in Measurements with lesson 1 (plain QPSK): it is lower, which is why OQPSK is friendlier to nonlinear power amplifiers. On the Eye tab the Q traces are centred half a symbol after the I traces.
